### Method reminder

Link each drawback of an old generation to its hardware cause, then to the technology that solved it.

### Solution

The first generation computers were built with **vacuum tubes**. Two disadvantages (any two):

- very large machines, filling a whole room;
- high electricity consumption and a lot of heat produced, so they needed cooling;
- frequent failures, because tubes burned out;
- programmed in machine language, slow and difficult to use.

The vacuum tube was replaced by the **transistor** (second generation).
